== DONE 1: 5 GB = hard quit for every download command (commit 160dad3) ==

- --main, --download, --process, --scribd, --phatmal check free space before each file.
  under 5 GB -> [disk-full] only X GB free, under the 5.0 GB kept for the system
  -> exit 1, failure email right away (names the part). rerun resumes after you free space.
- the 5 GB is in one place: python/bin/disk_floor.py (DISK_FLOOR).
- --process: the old "pause until uploads free space" is DELETED, and so is the
  uploader restarting on a tight disk. a full disk now ends the night with an error.
  !! this means: if uploads are slower than downloads, the night run quits at 5 GB
  even when uploads still work. before, it waited for uploads. that is what
  "all flags" means to me - tell me "keep pause in --process" if you want the old way there.
- upload rule unchanged: 5 failed tries -> disk has room: stop uploading only;
  disk tight while downloading: quit entirely (exit with error).

== DONE 2: 3 retry turns after crawling (commit cf2594d) ==

- --download, --main, --process: when crawling has finished (all URLs found, all
  downloads tried), every URL in scan/failed.txt and scan/blocked.txt gets 3 turns:
  one try per URL per turn, line by line, no waiting.
  works -> saved like any download (python/pdfs, downloaded.txt, timeline) and its
  line is removed from failed.txt AND blocked.txt. fails -> next line. after turn 3 -> done.
- failed downloads are no error: exit 0, the finished email / night report gets
  "Retry (3 turns ...): R of N URL(s) recovered, L still failing."
- --process: the turns run before the last upload, so recovered files go to the host.
- the console looks like this:
    [retry] crawling finished: 4 URL(s) from scan/failed.txt and scan/blocked.txt get 3 turns
    [retry] turn 1/3: 4 URL(s)
    [retry-fail] .../books/flaky.pdf: ... (turn 1/3)
    [retry] turn 2/3: 4 URL(s)
    [retry-ok] .../books/flaky.pdf: saved flaky.pdf (turn 2/3); removed from scan/failed.txt and scan/blocked.txt
    [retry] done: 1 recovered, 3 still failing

== TESTED (real runs, local test sites, fake ssh host, local mail server) ==

- 5 GB: under 5 GB from the start -> --process, --download, --scribd, --phatmal each
  exit 1, nothing saved, failure email names their part. disk filling in --process
  -> [disk-full] -> exit 1 in seconds; --upload frees it; rerun finishes all 30 files.
- retry: a file failing twice then working -> recovered on turn 2. missing file, dead
  file, page without download -> exactly 1 try per turn, kept. next run with the site
  fixed -> recovered on turn 1, removed from both files; a 3rd run retries only the dead one.
- your scan .txt reminder: same records as your main branch code (f932217) in
  blocked.txt, failed.txt, downloaded.txt, timeline.log, uploaded-host.txt,
  crawl-*.jsonl. only difference: 2 new timeline rows (retry, retry-done). 23/23.
- all night checks: 35/35. retry checks: 14/14.
- NOT tested: real sites, a real full disk, real Hostinger mail.

